---Azure Blob Storage addon configuration.
---@class auth0.ClientAddonAzureBlob
---@field accountName? string Your Azure storage account name. Usually first segment in your Azure storage URL. e.g. `https://acme-org.blob.core.windows.net` would be the account name `acme-org`.
---@field storageAccessKey? string Access key associated with this storage account.
---@field containerName? string Container to request a token for. e.g. `my-container`.
---@field blobName? string Entity to request a token for. e.g. `my-blob`. If blank the computed SAS will apply to the entire storage container.
---@field expiration? number Expiration in minutes for the generated token (default of 5 minutes).
---@field signedIdentifier? string Shared access policy identifier defined in your storage account resource.
---@field blob_read? boolean Indicates if the issued token has permission to read the content, properties, metadata and block list. Use the blob as the source of a copy operation.
---@field blob_write? boolean Indicates if the issued token has permission to create or write content, properties, metadata, or block list. Snapshot or lease the blob. Resize the blob (page blob only). Use the blob as the destination of a copy operation within the same account.
---@field blob_delete? boolean Indicates if the issued token has permission to delete the blob.
---@field container_read? boolean Indicates if the issued token has permission to read the content, properties, metadata or block list of any blob in the container. Use any blob in the container as the source of a copy operation
---@field container_write? boolean Indicates that for any blob in the container if the issued token has permission to create or write content, properties, metadata, or block list. Snapshot or lease the blob. Resize the blob (page blob only). Use the blob as the destination of a copy operation within the same account.
---@field container_delete? boolean Indicates if issued token has permission to delete any blob in the container.
---@field container_list? boolean Indicates if the issued token has permission to list blobs in the container.
---@field [string] any

---Azure Storage Bus addon configuration.
---@class auth0.ClientAddonAzureSB
---@field namespace? string Your Azure Service Bus namespace. Usually the first segment of your Service Bus URL (e.g. `https://acme-org.servicebus.windows.net` would be `acme-org`).
---@field sasKeyName? string Your shared access policy name defined in your Service Bus entity.
---@field sasKey? string Primary Key associated with your shared access policy.
---@field entityPath? string Entity you want to request a token for. e.g. `my-queue`.'
---@field expiration? number Optional expiration in minutes for the generated token. Defaults to 5 minutes.
---@field [string] any

