---Native to Web SSO Configuration
---@class auth0.ClientSessionTransferConfiguration
---@field can_create_session_transfer_token? boolean Indicates whether an app can issue a Session Transfer Token through Token Exchange. If set to 'false', the app will not be able to issue a Session Transfer Token. Usually configured in the native application. Default value is `false`.
---@field enforce_cascade_revocation? boolean Indicates whether revoking the parent Refresh Token that initiated a Native to Web flow and was used to issue a Session Transfer Token should trigger a cascade revocation affecting its dependent child entities. Usually configured in the native application. Default value is `true`, applicable only in Native to Web SSO context.
---@field allowed_authentication_methods? auth0.ClientSessionTransferConfigurationAllowedAuthenticationMethodsList|distilled.Null Indicates whether an app can create a session from a Session Transfer Token received via indicated methods. Can include `cookie` and/or `query`. Usually configured in the web application. Default value is an empty array [].
---@field enforce_device_binding? auth0.ClientSessionTransferDeviceBindingEnum|string
---@field allow_refresh_token? boolean Indicates whether Refresh Tokens are allowed to be issued when authenticating with a Session Transfer Token. Usually configured in the web application. Default value is `false`.
---@field enforce_online_refresh_tokens? boolean Indicates whether Refresh Tokens created during a Native to Web session are tied to that session's lifetime. This determines if such refresh tokens should be automatically revoked when their corresponding sessions are. Usually configured in the web application. Default value is `true`, applicable only in Native to Web SSO context.
---@field delegation? auth0.ClientSessionTransferDelegationConfiguration|distilled.Null

---Indicates whether an app can create a session from a Session Transfer Token received via indicated methods. Can include `cookie` and/or `query`. Usually configured in the web application. Default value is an empty array [].
---@alias auth0.ClientSessionTransferConfigurationAllowedAuthenticationMethodsList (auth0.ClientSessionTransferAllowedAuthenticationMethodsEnum|string)[]

---Configuration for delegation (impersonation) access using Session Transfer Tokens
---@class auth0.ClientSessionTransferDelegationConfiguration
---@field allow_delegated_access? boolean Indicates whether delegation (impersonation) access is allowed using Session Transfer Tokens. Default value is `false`.
---@field enforce_device_binding? auth0.ClientSessionTransferDelegationDeviceBindingEnum|string

---Indicates the device binding enforcement for delegation (impersonation) access. The only supported value is `ip`, which enforces device binding by IP, meaning consumption of the Session Transfer Token must be done from the same IP as the issuer.
---@alias auth0.ClientSessionTransferDelegationDeviceBindingEnum "ip"

---Indicates whether device binding security should be enforced for the app. If set to 'ip', the app will enforce device binding by IP, meaning that consumption of Session Transfer Token must be done from the same IP of the issuer. Likewise, if set to 'asn', device binding is enforced by ASN, meaning consumption of Session Transfer Token must be done from the same ASN as the issuer. If set to 'none', device binding is not enforced. Usually configured in the web application. Default value is `ip`.
---@alias auth0.ClientSessionTransferDeviceBindingEnum "ip"|"asn"|"none"

