---@class auth0.CreateClientRequest
---@field name string Name of this client (min length: 1 character, does not allow `<` or `>`).
---@field description? string Free text description of this client (max length: 140 characters).
---@field logo_uri? string URL of the logo to display for this client. Recommended size is 150x150 pixels.
---@field callbacks? auth0.CreateClientRequestCallbacksList Comma-separated list of URLs whitelisted for Auth0 to use as a callback to the client after authentication.
---@field oidc_logout? auth0.ClientOIDCBackchannelLogoutSettings
---@field oidc_backchannel_logout? auth0.ClientOIDCBackchannelLogoutSettings Configuration for OIDC backchannel logout (deprecated, in favor of oidc_logout)
---@field session_transfer? auth0.ClientSessionTransferConfiguration|distilled.Null
---@field allowed_origins? auth0.CreateClientRequestAllowedOriginsList Comma-separated list of URLs allowed to make requests from JavaScript to Auth0 API (typically used with CORS). By default, all your callback URLs will be allowed. This field allows you to enter other origins if necessary. You can also use wildcards at the subdomain level (e.g., https://*.contoso.com). Query strings and hash information are not taken into account when validating these URLs.
---@field web_origins? auth0.CreateClientRequestWebOriginsList Comma-separated list of allowed origins for use with <a href='https://auth0.com/docs/cross-origin-authentication'>Cross-Origin Authentication</a>, <a href='https://auth0.com/docs/flows/concepts/device-auth'>Device Flow</a>, and <a href='https://auth0.com/docs/protocols/oauth2#how-response-mode-works'>web message response mode</a>.
---@field client_aliases? auth0.CreateClientRequestClientAliasesList List of audiences/realms for SAML protocol. Used by the wsfed addon.
---@field allowed_clients? auth0.CreateClientRequestAllowedClientsList List of allow clients and API ids that are allowed to make delegation requests. Empty means all all your clients are allowed.
---@field allowed_logout_urls? auth0.CreateClientRequestAllowedLogoutUrlsList Comma-separated list of URLs that are valid to redirect to after logout from Auth0. Wildcards are allowed for subdomains.
---@field grant_types? auth0.CreateClientRequestGrantTypesList List of grant types supported for this application. Can include `authorization_code`, `implicit`, `refresh_token`, `client_credentials`, `password`, `http://auth0.com/oauth/grant-type/password-realm`, `http://auth0.com/oauth/grant-type/mfa-oob`, `http://auth0.com/oauth/grant-type/mfa-otp`, `http://auth0.com/oauth/grant-type/mfa-recovery-code`, `urn:openid:params:grant-type:ciba`, `urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code`, and `urn:auth0:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange:federated-connection-access-token`.
---@field token_endpoint_auth_method? auth0.ClientTokenEndpointAuthMethodEnum|string
---@field is_token_endpoint_ip_header_trusted? boolean If true, trust that the IP specified in the `auth0-forwarded-for` header is the end-user's IP for brute-force-protection on token endpoint.
---@field app_type? auth0.ClientAppTypeEnum|string
---@field is_first_party? boolean Whether this client a first party client or not
---@field oidc_conformant? boolean Whether this client conforms to <a href='https://auth0.com/docs/api-auth/tutorials/adoption'>strict OIDC specifications</a> (true) or uses legacy features (false).
---@field jwt_configuration? auth0.ClientJwtConfiguration
---@field encryption_key? auth0.ClientEncryptionKey|distilled.Null
---@field sso? boolean Applies only to SSO clients and determines whether Auth0 will handle Single Sign On (true) or whether the Identity Provider will (false).
---@field cross_origin_authentication? boolean Whether this client can be used to make cross-origin authentication requests (true) or it is not allowed to make such requests (false).
---@field cross_origin_loc? string URL of the location in your site where the cross origin verification takes place for the cross-origin auth flow when performing Auth in your own domain instead of Auth0 hosted login page.
---@field sso_disabled? boolean <code>true</code> to disable Single Sign On, <code>false</code> otherwise (default: <code>false</code>)
---@field custom_login_page_on? boolean <code>true</code> if the custom login page is to be used, <code>false</code> otherwise. Defaults to <code>true</code>
---@field custom_login_page? string The content (HTML, CSS, JS) of the custom login page.
---@field custom_login_page_preview? string The content (HTML, CSS, JS) of the custom login page. (Used on Previews)
---@field form_template? string HTML form template to be used for WS-Federation.
---@field addons? auth0.ClientAddons
---@field client_metadata? auth0.ClientMetadata
---@field mobile? auth0.ClientMobile
---@field initiate_login_uri? string Initiate login uri, must be https
---@field native_social_login? auth0.NativeSocialLogin
---@field fedcm_login? auth0.FedCMLogin
---@field refresh_token? auth0.ClientRefreshTokenConfiguration|distilled.Null
---@field default_organization? auth0.ClientDefaultOrganization|distilled.Null
---@field organization_usage? auth0.ClientOrganizationUsageEnum|string
---@field organization_require_behavior? auth0.ClientOrganizationRequireBehaviorEnum|string
---@field organization_discovery_methods? auth0.CreateClientRequestOrganizationDiscoveryMethodsList Defines the available methods for organization discovery during the `pre_login_prompt`. Users can discover their organization either by `email`, `organization_name` or both.
---@field client_authentication_methods? auth0.ClientCreateAuthenticationMethod
---@field require_pushed_authorization_requests? boolean Makes the use of Pushed Authorization Requests mandatory for this client
---@field require_proof_of_possession? boolean Makes the use of Proof-of-Possession mandatory for this client
---@field signed_request_object? auth0.ClientSignedRequestObjectWithPublicKey
