---@class auth0.CreateConnectionRequest
---@field name string The name of the connection. Must start and end with an alphanumeric character and can only contain alphanumeric characters and '-'. Max length 128
---@field display_name? string Connection name used in the new universal login experience
---@field strategy auth0.ConnectionIdentityProviderEnum|string
---@field options? auth0.ConnectionPropertiesOptions
---@field enabled_clients? auth0.CreateConnectionRequestEnabledClientsList Use of this property is NOT RECOMMENDED. Use the PATCH /v2/connections/{id}/clients endpoint to enable the connection for a set of clients.
---@field is_domain_connection? boolean <code>true</code> promotes to a domain-level connection so that third-party applications can use it. <code>false</code> does not promote the connection, so only first-party applications with the connection enabled can use it. (Defaults to <code>false</code>.)
---@field show_as_button? boolean Enables showing a button for the connection in the login page (new experience only). If false, it will be usable only by HRD. (Defaults to <code>false</code>.)
---@field realms? auth0.CreateConnectionRequestRealmsList Defines the realms for which the connection will be used (ie: email domains). If the array is empty or the property is not specified, the connection name will be added as realm.
---@field metadata? auth0.ConnectionsMetadata
---@field authentication? auth0.ConnectionAuthenticationPurpose
---@field connected_accounts? auth0.ConnectionConnectedAccountsPurpose
---@field cross_app_access_requesting_app? auth0.CrossAppAccessRequestingApp
---@field cross_app_access_resource_app? auth0.CreateCrossAppAccessResourceApp

