---@class auth0.GetClientGrantsRequest
---@field per_page? number Number of results per page.
---@field page? number Page index of the results to return. First page is 0.
---@field include_totals? boolean Return results inside an object that contains the total result count (true) or as a direct array of results (false, default).
---@field from? string Optional Id from which to start selection.
---@field take? number Number of results per page. Defaults to 50.
---@field audience? string Optional filter on audience.
---@field client_id? string Optional filter on client_id.
---@field allow_any_organization? boolean Optional filter on allow_any_organization.
---@field subject_type? auth0.ClientGrantSubjectTypeEnum|string The type of application access the client grant allows.
---@field default_for? auth0.ClientGrantDefaultForEnum|string Applies this client grant as the default for all clients in the specified group. The only accepted value is <a href="https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/applications/application-access-to-apis-client-grants#default-permissions-for-third-party-applications">`third_party_clients`</a>, which applies the grant to all third-party clients. Per-client grants for the same audience take precedence. Mutually exclusive with `client_id`.

---@class auth0.GetClientGrantsSearchRequest
---@field q? string Filter expression in SCIM or Lucene syntax (depending on parser parameter). SCIM examples: `audience eq "https://api.example.com"`, `client_id eq "cli_abc"`, `subject_type eq "client"`, `allow_any_organization eq true`, `default_for eq "third_party_clients"`, `audience co "example" and organization_id eq "org_123"`. SCIM operators: eq, ne, sw, ew, co, pr, gt, ge, lt, le, and, or. <br /><br /><b>Supported Fields</b>:<ul><li><i>audience</i> - Filter by audience (eq, ne, sw, co, ew, pr)</li><li><i>client_id</i> - Filter by client ID (eq, ne, sw, pr)</li><li><i>subject_type</i> - Filter by subject type (eq, ne, sw, pr)</li><li><i>allow_any_organization</i> - Filter by allow_any_organization (eq, ne, pr)</li><li><i>organization_id</i> - Filter by organization ID (eq, ne, sw, pr)</li><li><i>updated_at</i> - Filter by last update date (eq, ne, gt, ge, lt, le, pr)</li><li><i>default_for</i> - Filter by default grant group (eq, ne, sw, pr)</li></ul>Maximum 5 filter operations per query. Results are eventually consistent and may not reflect recent updates.
---@field parser? auth0.SearchParserEnum|string Query parser to use for the filter expression. Use "scim" for SCIM filter syntax or "lucene" for Lucene query syntax (default).
---@field fields? string Comma-separated list of fields to include or exclude in the response. Works with the include_fields parameter to control projection mode.
---@field include_fields? boolean Controls field projection mode. Set to true to include only fields specified in the fields parameter. Set to false to exclude fields specified in the fields parameter. Defaults to true if not specified.
---@field take? number Maximum number of results to return per page (1-100). Defaults to 50.
---@field from? string Cursor for the next page of results. Use the value from the next field in the previous response.
---@field sort? auth0.ClientGrantSortFieldEnum|string Field name to sort results by in ascending order. Defaults to insertion order (oldest first) if not provided.

