---@field client_id? string ID of the client (application). If provided for tenants using the New Universal Login experience, the email template and UI displays application details, and the user is prompted to redirect to the application's <a target='' href='https://auth0.com/docs/authenticate/login/auth0-universal-login/configure-default-login-routes#completing-the-password-reset-flow'>default login route</a> after the ticket is used. client_id is required to use the <a target='' href='https://auth0.com/docs/customize/actions/flows-and-triggers/post-change-password-flow'>Password Reset Post Challenge</a> trigger.
---@field organization_id? string (Optional) Organization ID – the ID of the Organization. If provided, organization parameters will be made available to the email template and organization branding will be applied to the prompt. In addition, the redirect link in the prompt will include organization_id and organization_name query string parameters.
---@field connection_id? string ID of the connection. If provided, allows the user to be specified using email instead of user_id. If you set this value, you must also send the email parameter. You cannot send user_id when specifying a connection_id.
---@field email? string Email address of the user for whom the tickets should be created. Requires the connection_id parameter. Cannot be specified when using user_id.
---@field ttl_sec? number Number of seconds for which the ticket is valid before expiration. If unspecified or set to 0, this value defaults to 432000 seconds (5 days).
---@field mark_email_as_verified? boolean Whether to set the email_verified attribute to true (true) or whether it should not be updated (false).
---@field includeEmailInRedirect? boolean Whether to include the email address as part of the returnUrl in the reset_email (true), or not (false).
---@field identity? auth0.ChangePasswordTicketIdentity

